From 5f8f326a4ea4eda36b18d52aa368e8f8ec6736ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:02:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] phase3: task 2a EDU data spine -- stat_sec schema +
 ranged rows + spawn mapping

- BattleEduParser: stat_sec joins the schema (11-value arity, same kinds as
  stat_pri, canonical position after stat_pri) -> SchemaFieldCount 15. T0.2
  golden RE-SIGNED (disclosed): fixture + embedded GoldenCanonical + every
  inline edge fixture carry the field.
- golden_edu_v1.txt: +2 ranged rows (Peasant Archers: arrow/120m/25 ammo,
  arced; Mercenary Crossbowmen: bolt/160m/18 ammo, flat); the 2 melee rows
  carry stat_sec mirroring stat_pri. Values are A6 placeholders (ADR-30).
- FBattleRowStats::FromEdu: the missile branch (spec ranged-stack section 6)
  -- stat_pri is the missile weapon when its missile slot != 'no'; stat_sec
  is then the melee backup. Unknown missile tokens fail loudly. bSkirmishDefault
  from class 'missile' (A8).
- UBattleSpawnLibrary: FRangedStateFragment rides ranged-capable compositions
  only (arch section 3.2; bRanged branch in the archetype build + fixup with
  the StaggeredPhaseOffset reload scatter); registry SetUnitSkirmishDefault
  stamp at spawn. Archetype growth MEASURED by SpawnComposition (one ranged
  composition expected; itemized in the phase report, F6 disclosed re-sign).
- BattleUnitTrait (Route B parity): Kind/RangedRangeM/AmmoPerMan properties
  + conditional fragment stamp; BuildT0Configs authors the two ranged configs.
- MassBattleEduTests: counts + goldens re-signed; ranged spot checks
  (missile kind, range, ammo, stat_sec melee attack); stat_sec arity +
  missing-field edge cases.
- MassBattleCombatTests SpawnComposition: ranged-roster fragment
  presence/absence checks + archetype growth evidence line.

MUST re-run on the UE machine: unit tier (Battle.Data.* re-signed goldens,
SpawnComposition, all spawn-dependent suites) + func tier (unchanged
expectations: the two task-0 skeletons red only). Static patch: brace-
balanced, include-complete; no engine build was available at author time.
